{"name":"San Francisco Fog","hex":"#c4c2bc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"san","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sanskrit."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Ancient Greek letter representing /s/ (uppercase Ϻ, lowercase ϻ), originally used in some dialects instead of sigma."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/san"},{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"San Francisco fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a common weather phenomenon in the San Francisco Bay Area and the entire coastline of California extending south to the northwest coast of the Baja California Peninsula. The frequency of fog and low-lying stratus clouds is due to a combination of factors particular to the region that are especially prevalent in the summer. Another type of fog, tule fog, can occur during the winter. There are occasions when both types can coincide in the Bay Area. Some studies suggest that the prevalence of fog in the San Francisco Bay Area has decreased since 1951; however, some suggest these data are insufficient, or even suggest contrary results. Decreases in fog, if occurring, are likely due to climate change and anthropogenic change."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Golden_Fog%2C_San_Francisco.jpg/330px-Golden_Fog%2C_San_Francisco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_fog"},{"title":"San Francisco Fog RFC","blocks":[{"text":"San Francisco Fog Rugby Football Club (RFC), also known as \"The Fog\", is a rugby union football club in San Francisco, California. It is the first such team in the western United States established specifically to actively reach out to traditionally under-represented groups in rugby, such as people of color, gay men, and women. It welcomes players who do not fit into those categories. The club has over 100 members."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Fog_RFC"},{"title":"San Francisco","blocks":[{"text":"San Francisco, officially the City and County of San Francisco, is the 17th-most populous city and second-densest large city in the United States, with a population of 826,079 in 2025. It is the fourth-largest city in California. Some 4.6 million residents live in the city's metropolitan statistical area, which is the 13th-largest in the United States. Around 9.2 million live in the San Jose–San Francisco–Oakland combined statistical area, the fifth-largest in the United States. San Francisco is a global center for technology and finance, and is well-known for its affluence, eclectic architecture, and mild climate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Zeppelin-ride-020100925-195_%285029394846%29.jpg/330px-Zeppelin-ride-020100925-195_%285029394846%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco"},{"title":"Francisco","blocks":[{"text":"Francisco is the Spanish and Portuguese form of the masculine given name Franciscus."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francisco"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/San_francisco_in_fog_with_rays.jpg/500px-San_francisco_in_fog_with_rays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/San_francisco_in_fog_with_rays.jpg/1280px-San_francisco_in_fog_with_rays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum